{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq8zls6ya54","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Zonoid launch messaging + README hero (canonical copy)","summary":"Canonical launch copy for Zonoid (the open-sourced orchestrator). One-liner: \"Zonoid — a local-first task graph and bi-temporal knowledge graph for Claude Code agents. Context flows between tasks along typed edges, decisions survive sessions, and every claim links to a checked-in benchmark — including the ones that came back null.\" Tagline: \"Every segment adds to the solid.\" Moat sentence: the only system where memory is a byproduct of task execution (completion-produced, deterministically invalidated by supersede/judge/benchmark with provenance, routed via typed edges under a token budget) and the only one publishing its own nulls. README hero = h1 Zonoid + one-liner + tagline + badges (Apache-2.0, v0.9.0, macOS|Linux, no-telemetry) + DAG GIF + \"60 seconds: what you get\" (native-task graph / two-tier handoff / bi-temporal as_of KB / measure-judge-merge / local-first) + 2-command plugin quickstart. CONSTRAINTS: name Zonoid; npm scoped @zonoid/cli (bare zonoid blocked by typosquat filter); NO retracted v1-v7 ON/OFF numbers (1.63x->1.03x, 1.29x, 2.2x are retracted-contaminated); surviving receipts only = held-out wins (cold 0/10 & 0/8 -> warm 8.8/10 & 8/8), as_of 1.0 vs 0.6 recall@5, retrieval 0.91/0.82; never neural/swarm/unmeasured multipliers; gated retrieval LIVE, auto-consult roadmap; the self-caught-contamination story IS used as an asset. Show HN title: \"Show HN: Zonoid – a task graph that remembers, and the benchmark where memory made agents worse\". Reddit r/ClaudeAI: \"I measured whether memory actually helps Claude Code. Sometimes it doesn't. Data inside.\" DELIVERY NOTE: full copy deck could not be written to scratch/competitive/E1-launch-messaging.md — orch-gate-bash + Write permission both blocked file mutation for this background worker despite a valid task claim; full deck is in this w